Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.75,0:00:06.09,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Am I imagining things, or have you \Nbeen neglecting my revenge lately?!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.47,0:00:08.48,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,W-Well...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.29,0:00:11.74,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,It's been a month since the kidnapping.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.44,0:00:19.44,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,Kate's testimony revealed several facts \Nabout the mysterious Daeg Gallus.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.77,0:00:22.88,Flashback,Connie,0,0,0,,Kiriki kirikuku.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.19,0:00:28.62,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,The "spell" Lady Lily left behind was \None of the organization's passwords.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.29,0:00:32.71,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,Their goal is to steal her key.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.44,0:00:37.96,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,I decided to give it to His Lordship \Nand ask him to investigate it himself.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.59,0:00:42.90,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,The kidnapper had a sun tattoo,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.90,0:00:45.40,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,so we think he was\N a member of Daeg Gallus,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.10,0:00:49.76,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,but someone assassinated him in jail \Nbefore he could be questioned.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.64,0:00:55.03,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,Witnesses placed \NCrown Princess Cecilia in the vicinity.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.13,0:01:00.15,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Now tell me, \Nwhy are we calling on Abigail?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.63,0:01:03.55,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,To meet with Viscountess Aisha Huxley.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:03.55,0:01:07.51,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,You said you had business with her \Nat Baroness Godwin's ball, remember?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.82,0:01:10.26,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Oh, her.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.78,0:01:15.96,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,She might ignore a request\N for a meeting from a girl like me,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.57,0:01:20.13,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,so I thought I'd ask \Nthe House of O'Brian for a favor.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.66,0:01:23.02,Default,Abigail,0,0,0,,It's so good to see you, Constance.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:23.84,0:01:26.75,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,It's been too long, Lady Abigail.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:29.03,0:01:31.27,Default,Lucia,0,0,0,,My, but you are pretty!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:31.55,0:01:34.94,Default,Lucia,0,0,0,,Those amethyst eyes \Nand that scarlet dress...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:35.28,0:01:37.94,Default,Lucia,0,0,0,,Why, you could be a princess!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:38.28,0:01:39.49,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:39.98,0:01:42.78,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,I see you have taste, girl.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:42.78,0:01:45.99,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,W-Wait... Huh? What?!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:17.60,0:03:19.50,Default,Abigail,0,0,0,,I understand the situation.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:19.82,0:03:23.77,Default,Abigail,0,0,0,,I'll see to it that you receive\N an invitation from the Huxleys soon.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:25.05,0:03:27.51,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,You mean you believe me?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:27.51,0:03:30.49,Default,Abigail,0,0,0,,You've puzzled me \Nall the while I've known you.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:30.49,0:03:32.69,Default,Abigail,0,0,0,,But if Scarlett's by your side,\N that explains it.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:33.37,0:03:36.45,Default,Abigail,0,0,0,,Say, Scarlett, can you hear me?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:36.45,0:03:38.58,Default,Lucia,0,0,0,,She's over there, Abby!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:38.58,0:03:40.05,Default,Abigail,0,0,0,,Thank you, Lucia.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.29,0:03:46.79,Default,Abigail,0,0,0,,Your execution pained me deeply, \Nso allow me to assist you.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:46.79,0:03:51.54,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Really? I wish you'd confine your jokes \Nto that squashed frog you call a face.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:51.97,0:03:56.03,Default,Lucia,0,0,0,,Um... She says, yes, she understands!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:57.04,0:04:00.03,Default,Abigail,0,0,0,,I don't doubt \Nshe's insulting me as we speak.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:00.31,0:04:05.04,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,I had no idea that anyone but me \Ncould see Scarlett.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:05.04,0:04:08.65,Default,Abigail,0,0,0,,My niece Lucia here\N was born with keen intuition.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:08.65,0:04:11.73,Default,Abigail,0,0,0,,If anyone else has eyes \Nlike hers, it would be...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:11.73,0:04:16.81,Default,Abigail,0,0,0,,Viscount Hamsworth, I suppose. \NThey say he has the goddesses' favor.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.81,0:04:18.71,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Does he really?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:19.56,0:04:23.56,Default,Abigail,0,0,0,,I've heard tell that the viscount \Ncan see unearthly beings.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:25.26,0:04:28.24,Flashback,Hamsworth,0,0,0,,Do you not think so, my lady?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.71,0:04:31.08,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,It couldn't be... Could it?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:31.33,0:04:34.32,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Forget that nouveau riche hog.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:34.32,0:04:35.57,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,We're leaving, Connie.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:36.86,0:04:41.13,Default,Abigail,0,0,0,,I do hope you'll speak \Nto your fiancé about my request.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:41.13,0:04:42.59,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Oh, yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:43.01,0:04:44.72,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Now, if you'll excuse me!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:49.45,0:04:53.16,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Teresa Jennings lost her life\N in an attempted murder-suicide.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:53.74,0:04:57.98,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Her husband, Kevin Jennings, \Nhas become an invalid.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:00.05,0:05:02.81,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,As far as Lady Abigail \Nwas able to discover,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:03.23,0:05:07.10,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Daeg Gallus is selling the \Nhallucinogen "Jackal's Paradise."
Dialogue: 0,0:05:07.45,0:05:12.94,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Forget all that and get what happened \Nten years ago out of Aisha.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.32,0:05:17.11,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Speaking of which,\N what was Aisha Huxley like?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:17.65,0:05:21.46,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Well, she used to be a gloomy, plain girl.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:21.46,0:05:25.34,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,You could say she was part of \Nmy entourage. Or a fan, I suppose.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:26.05,0:05:30.42,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,If I wore a red dress, so would Aisha.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:30.42,0:05:34.67,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,If I wore blue, she would too.\N In a similar style, no less.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:34.67,0:05:36.34,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,She'd even do her hair like mine.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:36.84,0:05:41.57,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,And just the once, she looked me \Nin the eye and spoke to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:43.22,0:05:44.98,Flashback,Aisha,0,0,0,,I want to be you.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:45.99,0:05:47.95,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,And how did you reply?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.41,0:05:50.52,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Why, that should be obvious.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:50.86,0:05:55.49,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,The world doesn't need \N{\i1}two{\i0} Scarlett Castiels.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:59.84,0:06:01.45,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,Duke Castiel.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:02.34,0:06:04.25,Default,Adolphus,0,0,0,,Oh, Randolph.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.10,0:06:08.51,Main - Top,Adolphus,0,0,0,,What's this urgent business you mentioned?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.51,0:06:10.97,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,Permit me to be blunt.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:11.37,0:06:14.65,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,I want to know \Nabout the Holy Grail of Eris.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:16.74,0:06:19.84,Default,Adolphus,0,0,0,,Why, whatever could that be?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:19.84,0:06:22.28,Default,Adolphus,0,0,0,,I'm sorry to say\N the term is unfamiliar to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:22.84,0:06:24.74,Default,Adolphus,0,0,0,,Will that be all?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:25.31,0:06:27.77,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,Yes, for the time being.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.74,0:06:31.98,Default,Adolphus,0,0,0,,A friendly word of warning.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.98,0:06:36.06,Default,Adolphus,0,0,0,,Finish building your hand \Nbefore you try to play it.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:36.06,0:06:38.79,Default,Adolphus,0,0,0,,That is the secret to a long life.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:44.45,0:06:46.68,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Let's go over what we know.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:47.00,0:06:52.27,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,We'll start with the attempt to poison \NCrown Princess Cecilia ten years ago,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:52.58,0:06:56.50,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,when they found poison \Nin one of her house's water jars.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:57.33,0:07:01.26,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,What made people \Nsuspect you to begin with?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:01.55,0:07:04.27,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,It went just as that schemer told you.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:04.27,0:07:09.45,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,They found a moonbowstone \Nearring just like mine
Dialogue: 0,0:07:09.45,0:07:12.27,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,lying beside the Luzes' water store.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:12.61,0:07:17.89,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,As ill luck would have it, I'd called \Nat the house just hours earlier.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:24.30,0:07:27.85,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Was the earring really yours?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:27.85,0:07:33.31,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,No, I had both of mine \Nwhen I first fell under suspicion.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:33.52,0:07:34.93,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,And did you...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:34.93,0:07:37.31,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Tell the investigators? Of course.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:37.66,0:07:42.55,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Everything I wore was one-of-a-kind\Nfrom the hands of master craftsmen.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:42.82,0:07:46.95,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Inquiring at their workshops \Nwould have substantiated as much.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:47.67,0:07:51.27,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Then why weren't you \Ncleared of suspicion?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.81,0:07:57.85,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,I was told that, upon inspection, \None of my earrings turned out to be fake.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:57.85,0:08:02.58,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,They claimed I'd anticipated the\N investigation and prepared a replacement.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:02.95,0:08:04.14,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,In other words,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:04.14,0:08:07.12,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,someone swapped one of mine
Dialogue: 0,0:08:07.12,0:08:11.58,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,for the one found at the Luze estate\Nwhile it was in the Security Force's safe.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:12.04,0:08:13.59,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Who would do such a thing?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:13.59,0:08:16.44,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,I don't know. But in the end,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:16.93,0:08:22.20,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,the king authorized a search of my home.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:22.20,0:08:26.98,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,No one would dare touch the Castiel \Nresidence without a royal order.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:27.47,0:08:32.72,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Then, as you know, a half-empty vial \Nof poison turned up in my chambers,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:32.72,0:08:35.04,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,and they marched me off to a cell.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:35.74,0:08:39.39,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Did you suspect Crown Princess Cecilia?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:39.39,0:08:44.24,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,I suppose. She did benefit \Nthe most from my death.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:44.56,0:08:49.00,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,So until just recently, I thought \Nshe'd orchestrated the whole thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:49.27,0:08:51.01,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Only until recently?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:51.01,0:08:54.39,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,To be frank, I'm not sure anymore.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:54.39,0:08:58.77,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,I mean, she doesn't seem \Nthe least bit satisfied.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:59.44,0:09:03.69,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,After ten whole years, she seems \Nto loathe Enrique as much as ever.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:03.69,0:09:06.85,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,And she doesn't seem attached \Nto wealth or power, either.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:07.61,0:09:11.83,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,I wonder what she's trying to achieve.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:13.27,0:09:16.09,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,I suppose we're still far from the truth.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:16.09,0:09:19.77,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,True. But we have more than \Nthe events of ten years ago to go on.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:19.77,0:09:24.79,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Something is happening now, and we can \Nbe certain Cecilia has a hand in it.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:25.10,0:09:27.78,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Do you remember what \Nthat red-haired reporter woman said?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:28.23,0:09:32.80,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Cecilia Luze was a whore's daughter\N raised in an orphanage.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:33.18,0:09:37.79,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,And Kevin Jennings, who got close \Nto the truth, wound up an addict.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:37.79,0:09:39.33,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Oh, that's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:41.01,0:09:47.19,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,That merchant visiting her the very day\Nthe seventh prince of Faris was abducted
Dialogue: 0,0:09:47.19,0:09:49.60,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,lines up too perfectly to be happenstance.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:49.60,0:09:53.61,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,The merchant's name was, \Num... Vado, wasn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:54.07,0:10:00.07,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Come to think of it, didn't the kidnapper \Nhave an accomplice called Salvador?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:00.07,0:10:04.01,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,The names bear a similarity on paper. \NCoincidence, do you think?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:05.35,0:10:08.16,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,If they are the same person,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:08.16,0:10:12.33,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,then we can assume Cecilia is \Ninvolved with Daeg Gallus as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:12.98,0:10:18.71,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,And that they have a hand in distributing \NJackal's Paradise on Rosenkreuz Street.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:19.44,0:10:24.96,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,That young lady who collapsed at \Nthe Earl John Doe Ball, Kiara Grafton,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:25.26,0:10:27.05,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,used that hallucinogen, didn't she?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:28.22,0:10:30.20,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,And so did Kevin Jennings.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:31.48,0:10:35.99,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Then Prince Ulysses's abduction,\NKate's kidnapping,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:35.99,0:10:42.05,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,and the spread of Jackal's Paradise \Nare all Daeg Gallus's doing?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:42.49,0:10:45.33,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,You're forgetting one important thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:46.57,0:10:49.99,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Daeg Gallus attacked {\i1}you{\i0} as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:51.48,0:10:56.01,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Kate Lorraine's kidnapper \Nwas after Lily's key, wasn't he?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:56.01,0:10:57.19,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:57.76,0:11:03.19,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,I just said that something's afoot now,\Nbut that isn't precisely correct.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:04.01,0:11:09.28,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Something has {\i1}been{\i0} afoot \Nfor the past ten years...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:09.82,0:11:12.22,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,right here in Adelbide.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:13.01,0:11:16.67,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,I'd be surprised if it had \Nnothing to do with my execution.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:18.03,0:11:19.05,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,True.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:20.92,0:11:25.40,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,Whatever it is, Lady Lily probably \Nlost her life because of it.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:25.99,0:11:31.00,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,"Destroy the Holy Grail of Eris"\N was her final message.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:32.01,0:11:33.53,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,We still don't know what it means.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:38.91,0:11:40.68,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Um, Your Lordship...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:40.68,0:11:41.49,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,Yes?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:42.00,0:11:45.81,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,I realize we're to share information, \Nbut why at a museum?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:46.20,0:11:49.00,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,It holds donations from \Nthe Orlamunde family.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:49.46,0:11:51.84,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,I thought they might \Noffer a clue to the key.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:52.35,0:11:54.62,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,I visited here with Lily as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:55.96,0:11:57.32,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,Of course...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:57.69,0:12:00.98,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,They were on a first-name basis.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:02.90,0:12:04.24,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,Of course.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:04.83,0:12:07.24,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Learn some tact!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:08.33,0:12:14.84,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,Here lies one of the holy books Saint \NAnastasia received from the goddesses.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:16.11,0:12:18.51,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,What's wrong? Are you hungry?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:18.51,0:12:20.36,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Oh, no! I mean...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:23.34,0:12:26.97,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,As for Abigail's request, \N it will take some time.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:27.83,0:12:32.29,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,The crown princess owns the hospital \Nwhere Kevin Jennings is a patient.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:32.75,0:12:35.71,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,I'll need to go through \Nbothersome formalities.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:35.71,0:12:37.11,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,I understand.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:37.45,0:12:41.50,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Scarlett and I went over \Nwhat happened ten years ago,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:41.99,0:12:44.92,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,and she says her earring was switched.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:44.92,0:12:47.63,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,I read the file on the earrings.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:47.63,0:12:51.12,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,The one deemed an imitation \Nwasn't made of moonbowstone
Dialogue: 0,0:12:51.12,0:12:54.18,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,but rather a type of shell \Ncalled silver-shell.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:56.42,0:12:58.18,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,And what of the design?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:58.18,0:13:02.62,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,U-Um, Scarlett would like to know\N how the design compared.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:02.62,0:13:06.39,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,It was identical to her own earrings.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:06.95,0:13:09.98,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,Silver-shell doesn't circulate\N by many routes.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:09.98,0:13:14.31,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,I looked up who'd bought any at the time \Nand found a familiar name:
Dialogue: 0,0:13:14.89,0:13:17.15,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,the Spencer family.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:17.38,0:13:18.69,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Isn't that...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:18.69,0:13:20.34,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,It's Aisha's maiden name.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:21.14,0:13:26.15,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,The Spencers own several workshops \Nthat work with precious metals.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:26.62,0:13:31.77,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,I wouldn't be surprised if Aisha \Nhad replicas of my earrings made.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:32.15,0:13:36.03,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,You said you planned to visit \Nthe Huxleys to question her?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:36.03,0:13:37.38,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Y-Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:38.39,0:13:43.93,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,She may be involved with Daeg Gallus. \NDon't do anything rash.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:44.36,0:13:45.44,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,I won't.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:49.67,0:13:52.44,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,I still don't feel a thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:52.44,0:13:54.74,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,I don't remember anything either.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:55.97,0:13:59.64,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Was I really executed here?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:03.93,0:14:06.01,Main - Italics,Aisha,0,0,0,,Constance Grail...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:06.90,0:14:11.44,Main - Italics,Aisha,0,0,0,,I never dreamed she'd use \NAbigail O'Brian to get to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:16.70,0:14:23.39,Main - Italics,Aisha,0,0,0,,Why do people say such a dull girl\Nreminds them of {\i0}the{\i1} Scarlett Castiel?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:27.08,0:14:29.98,Main - Italics,Aisha,0,0,0,,No one could ever take her place.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:30.58,0:14:33.30,Main - Italics,Aisha,0,0,0,,She is my goddess.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:34.12,0:14:36.72,Flashback,Scarlett,0,0,0,,You're Aisha Spencer, aren't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:38.91,0:14:42.85,Flashback,Scarlett,0,0,0,,You've been watching me.\N Just now, and earlier as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:42.85,0:14:44.60,Flashback,Scarlett,0,0,0,,What do you want?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:44.60,0:14:48.00,Flashback,Aisha,0,0,0,,How do you know, um, m-my name?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:48.42,0:14:52.37,Flashback,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Why, you introduced yourself \Nonce at some other party.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:52.37,0:14:54.63,Flashback,Aisha,0,0,0,,Y-You remember?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:54.63,0:14:56.29,Flashback,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Naturally.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:57.18,0:15:00.63,Flashback,Scarlett,0,0,0,,To whom do you imagine you're speaking?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:18.40,0:15:22.79,Default,Aisha,0,0,0,,Welcome, Miss Grail. I'm sorry \Nthe house isn't much to look at.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:22.79,0:15:23.89,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Not at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:24.44,0:15:28.90,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,I sincerely appreciate \Nyour invitation, Lady Huxley.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:30.13,0:15:33.80,Default,Aisha,0,0,0,,We're only lesser nobility.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:33.80,0:15:37.40,Default,Aisha,0,0,0,,I was shocked to receive \Na messenger from the O'Brians,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:37.68,0:15:41.64,Default,Aisha,0,0,0,,though he came bearing \Na request from the Grails.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:42.01,0:15:46.53,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,I hope you'll forgive me. \NI simply had to see you.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:46.99,0:15:50.92,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,If you don't mind, \NI'd like to ask you a question.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:50.92,0:15:54.36,Default,Aisha,0,0,0,,If it's one I can answer, go ahead.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:54.36,0:15:57.67,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,What is that smell?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:59.34,0:16:04.09,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,An acquaintance of mine has \Nan excellent nose and memory.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:04.09,0:16:06.93,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,She could tell the instant you appeared.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:07.31,0:16:11.20,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Tell me, Lady Huxley, why do you carry
Dialogue: 0,0:16:11.64,0:16:13.77,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,the scent of Jackal's Paradise?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:14.94,0:16:16.18,Main - Italics,Aisha,0,0,0,,She noticed?!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:17.29,0:16:19.41,Default,Aisha,0,0,0,,Whatever are you talking about?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:19.41,0:16:23.96,Default,Aisha,0,0,0,,Jackal's Paradise? That hallucinogen \Nthat was all the rage a decade ago?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:25.75,0:16:28.50,Default,Aisha,0,0,0,,You must be mistaken.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:28.50,0:16:33.72,Default,Aisha,0,0,0,,I am wearing a rare perfume today.\N Perhaps that's what you smell.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:33.72,0:16:38.34,Default,Aisha,0,0,0,,It comes from a distant land. \NI doubt you've heard of it.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:38.75,0:16:43.59,Default,Connie-S,0,0,0,,You're a laughably poor liar.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:44.85,0:16:47.33,Default,Aisha,0,0,0,,H-How terribly rude!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:47.33,0:16:49.36,Default,Aisha,0,0,0,,I won't stand for this! Leave at once!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:49.36,0:16:50.84,Default,Connie-S,0,0,0,,Dear me.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:50.84,0:16:53.40,Default,Connie-S,0,0,0,,Throwing a tantrum the moment \Nyour mischief comes to light?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:53.40,0:16:55.72,Default,Connie-S,0,0,0,,You behave like an undisciplined child.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:57.71,0:16:59.70,Main - Italics,Aisha,0,0,0,,What's come over me?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:00.11,0:17:04.90,Main - Italics,Aisha,0,0,0,,The same girl still stands before me,\N and yet I could almost...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:05.63,0:17:08.87,Default,Connie-S,0,0,0,,Mark my words, Aisha Spencer.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:09.24,0:17:13.89,Default,Connie-S,0,0,0,,Trying to fool me is far more \Noffensive than anything I said.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:16.19,0:17:20.39,Default,Connie-S,0,0,0,,To whom do you imagine you're speaking?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:20.95,0:17:23.36,Default,Aisha,0,0,0,,Scarlett...?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:24.34,0:17:28.64,Main - Italics,Aisha,0,0,0,,No, I'd never mistake anyone for her.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:28.64,0:17:34.33,Main - Italics,Aisha,0,0,0,,Ten years ago, Scarlett Castiel \Nwas the center of my world.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:35.40,0:17:39.52,Main - Italics,Aisha,0,0,0,,Her and her fiancé, Crown Prince Enrique.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:39.52,0:17:43.52,Main - Italics,Aisha,0,0,0,,They didn't share anything \Nas sweet as love,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:43.52,0:17:48.29,Main - Italics,Aisha,0,0,0,,but I noticed they were \Ncomfortable together, like siblings.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:48.78,0:17:51.77,Main - Italics,Aisha,0,0,0,,How I idolized them.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:52.52,0:17:55.66,Main - Italics,Aisha,0,0,0,,But then {\i0}she{\i1} came along.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:57.72,0:18:02.11,Main - Italics,Aisha,0,0,0,,Talk of their star-crossed love in \Ndefiance of status spread like wildfire.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:02.92,0:18:07.18,Main - Italics,Aisha,0,0,0,,I knew the rumors would become truth\N unless someone stopped them.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:07.18,0:18:11.19,Main - Italics,Aisha,0,0,0,,I thought that I had to do \Nsomething. And just then...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:12.82,0:18:14.94,Flashback,Aisha,0,0,0,,What happened, Sharon?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:14.94,0:18:18.59,Flashback,Aisha,0,0,0,,You look so much thinner \Nthan when I last saw you.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:18.94,0:18:20.27,Flashback,Sharon,0,0,0,,I used this.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:20.93,0:18:24.95,Flashback,Sharon,0,0,0,,It's supposed to be a kind of foreign \Nsmelling salts. Worked wonders, didn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:25.98,0:18:27.96,Flashback,Sharon,0,0,0,,One pinch is all it takes.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:28.47,0:18:30.91,Flashback,Sharon,0,0,0,,Taking too much is bad for your health.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:32.47,0:18:36.21,Main - Italics,Aisha,0,0,0,,I'd heard that Cecilia suffered from \Na naturally frail constitution.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:37.09,0:18:41.06,Main - Italics,Aisha,0,0,0,,If she took ill, she'd have\N to return to her family estate.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:43.31,0:18:48.25,Main - Italics,Aisha,0,0,0,,I put on my replica set of \NScarlett's moonbowstone earrings
Dialogue: 0,0:18:48.91,0:18:52.96,Main - Italics,Aisha,0,0,0,,and set out to pay a sympathy visit \Nto the Luze residence.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:53.48,0:18:59.49,Main - Italics,Aisha,0,0,0,,How was I to know Scarlett had come \Nand caused a scene mere hours earlier?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:02.49,0:19:04.49,Flashback - Italics,Aisha,0,0,0,,There it is!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:04.49,0:19:08.31,Flashback - Italics,Aisha,0,0,0,,I'll just pour the smelling salts \Ninto this water.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:09.25,0:19:14.61,Flashback - Italics,Aisha,0,0,0,,I'm doing this for Scarlett. \NI know she'd do the same.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:15.00,0:19:17.01,Flashback - Italics,Aisha,0,0,0,,If I were Scarlett, I'd...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:23.39,0:19:26.95,Flashback - Italics,Aisha,0,0,0,,If I do this, I can {\i0}become{\i1} Scarlett!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:30.38,0:19:32.88,Default,Connie-S,0,0,0,,So you poisoned the water.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:33.39,0:19:35.89,Default,Aisha,0,0,0,,I had no idea it was poison.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:37.40,0:19:39.11,Default,Aisha,0,0,0,,It's true!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:39.11,0:19:41.72,Default,Aisha,0,0,0,,I still have the bottle I used back then!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:41.72,0:19:45.40,Default,Aisha,0,0,0,,Check it and you'll see \Nit's only a slimming drug!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:45.40,0:19:47.14,Default,Aisha,0,0,0,,It wasn't my fault!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:47.14,0:19:49.91,Default,Aisha,0,0,0,,So please! Forgive me, Scarlett!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:50.17,0:19:51.68,Default,Connie-S,0,0,0,,You want my forgiveness?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:51.68,0:19:55.52,Default,Connie-S,0,0,0,,Then why did you not confess your crime?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:56.92,0:20:00.01,Default,Connie-S,0,0,0,,Whether it was poison or not \Nmakes no difference.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:00.01,0:20:04.42,Default,Connie-S,0,0,0,,Either way, you knew that I was innocent.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:06.14,0:20:10.68,Default,Connie-S,0,0,0,,I went to the executioner \Nbecause of the crime you committed.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:11.17,0:20:13.82,Default,Aisha,0,0,0,,I... I did it for you!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:13.82,0:20:17.53,Main - Top,Aisha,0,0,0,,You would have done the same thing \Nif you'd had the chance.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:17.53,0:20:19.06,Main - Top,Aisha,0,0,0,,So in your place, I—
Dialogue: 0,0:20:18.30,0:20:19.70,Default,Connie-S,0,0,0,,{\i1}I{\i0}...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:21.10,0:20:24.94,Default,Connie-S,0,0,0,,{\i1}I{\i0} would rather die than do \Nanything so disgraceful.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:27.03,0:20:32.78,Default,Connie-S,0,0,0,,Everything you did ten years ago,\N you did for yourself.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:33.71,0:20:38.71,Default,Connie-S,0,0,0,,Who do you think you are \Nto use me as your excuse?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:39.75,0:20:41.72,Default,Connie-S,0,0,0,,Aisha Spencer,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:42.35,0:20:45.41,Default,Connie-S,0,0,0,,just for you, I will ask one last time...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:45.96,0:20:50.10,Default,Connie-S,0,0,0,,To whom do you imagine you're speaking?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:51.79,0:20:54.24,Main - Italics,Aisha,0,0,0,,Deep down, I knew.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:55.32,0:20:59.48,Main - Italics,Aisha,0,0,0,,The answer has been staring me \Nin the face all this time.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:00.08,0:21:02.99,Main - Italics,Aisha,0,0,0,,I merely shut my eyes to it \Nto spare myself.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:03.56,0:21:06.09,Main - Italics,Aisha,0,0,0,,I caused it all.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:06.09,0:21:07.38,Main - Italics,Aisha,0,0,0,,I...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:08.07,0:21:10.31,Main - Italics,Aisha,0,0,0,,killed Scarlett!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:11.14,0:21:12.06,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,No!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:15.73,0:21:17.51,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,What good will dying do?!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:17.51,0:21:21.13,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Your death won't undo \Nwhat you did to Scarlett!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:25.71,0:21:28.93,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,You ought to live on and atone.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:32.42,0:21:34.12,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Lady Huxley?!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:40.21,0:21:44.90,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,A few days later, Aisha Huxley \Ncontacted the Mayflower Company,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:44.90,0:21:48.28,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,saying she wanted to confess her crimes.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:49.30,0:21:52.56,Default,Credits,0,0,0,,{\an8\fad(480,1)\fs12\bord1\fnArial\c&H351F51&\3c&H9985A7&\blur1\shad0\pos(153.286,329.428)}Translation:\h\h\h\h\h\h\hWilliam Varteresian
Dialogue: 1,0:21:50.72,0:21:51.96,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,Are you all right?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:55.03,0:21:56.34,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Your Lordship?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:55.56,0:21:59.06,Default,Credits,0,0,0,,{\fad(500,500)\fs10\bord1\fnArial\c&H1C0E48&\3c&H9087B4&\blur1\shad0\pos(85.286,204.857)}Subtitle Timing:\N{\fs12}Edgar Cruz\N\N\N{\fs10}Subtitle Editing:\N{\fs12}Riley Dalton
Dialogue: 0,0:21:57.08,0:21:59.40,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,He came for me...
Dialogue: 0,0:22:03.04,0:22:07.98,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,It was Aisha. She poisoned \Nthe Luzes' water jar.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:03.19,0:22:06.65,Default,Credits,0,0,0,,{\fad(500,500)\fs10\bord1\fnArial\c&H1C0E48&\3c&H9087B4&\blur1\shad0\pos(105.019,107.257)}Quality Check:\N{\fs12}SMR\N\N\N{\fs10}Translation Check:\N{\fs12}Sriram Gurunathan
Dialogue: 0,0:22:08.30,0:22:10.17,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,Do you have anything to prove it?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:10.17,0:22:12.52,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,She says she has the bottle of poison.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:12.52,0:22:16.71,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,From ten years ago?\NVerifying that will take time.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:17.08,0:22:21.49,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Also... she's been using\N Jackal's Paradise.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:21.49,0:22:24.70,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,So she does have dealings \Nwith Daeg Gallus after all.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:24.70,0:22:25.75,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:28.51,0:22:31.81,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,Give me the details another time, \Nwhen you feel more yourself.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:34.04,0:22:35.42,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,I'll escort you home.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:35.94,0:22:37.72,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,I would appreciate that.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:40.41,0:22:42.09,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Why did you stop her?!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:42.09,0:22:45.89,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,You should have just let her die!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:47.85,0:22:50.44,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Connie, you idiot! Why did you save her?!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:50.44,0:22:53.10,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,She was the one! It was her fault that I—
Dialogue: 0,0:22:53.10,0:22:54.40,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,And what if it was?!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:54.40,0:22:57.61,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,The nerve of her, \Nlooking to die over what you said!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:59.19,0:23:03.61,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,How could I let her make you \Nher excuse right to the end?!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:07.21,0:23:08.36,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Besides...
Dialogue: 0,0:23:08.91,0:23:13.12,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,we may lose our chance\N at more clues if Aisha dies now.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:13.84,0:23:17.65,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Your revenge is nowhere \Nnear complete, remember?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:18.61,0:23:24.38,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,There's whoever switched the earrings, \Nand Lady Lily, and Daeg Gallus.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:24.38,0:23:26.13,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,We haven't solved anything.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:27.26,0:23:30.64,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Listen, Scarlett. I...
Dialogue: 0,0:23:31.76,0:23:37.15,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,I'll spend the rest of my life\N ensuring that you have your revenge!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:39.26,0:23:43.26,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Sometimes, girl, \Nyou have a way with words.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:45.73,0:23:48.95,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,A line like that is too good for you.
